{
 "profile_id": "abaqulusi",
 "profile_name": "Abaqulusi Local Municipality (Vryheid, KZN)",
 "short_name": "Abaqulusi",
 "_doc": "ABAQULUSI (Vryheid, KZN) - TAX INVOICE/STATEMENT OF ACCOUNT. Same billing vendor as KwaDukuza (identical masthead grammar, METER READINGS / ACCOUNT DETAILS tables, 903001 VAT line, 120+ DAYS ageing row, REMITTANCE ADVICE footer), so the fingerprint is pinned on 'ABAQULUSI' plus VAT No. 4000791881 to keep the two apart.\n\nLAYOUT\n- Header block is label:value pairs on shared lines: 'Account Number:', 'Account Date: 28 JAN 2026', 'Tax Invoice No.:', 'Consumer Name: TELKOM SA', 'ERF Description:', 'Suburb:', 'Street:', 'Market Value:', 'Land Area:', 'Deposit:', 'Internet PIN:'. Consumer Name is ALWAYS 'TELKOM SA' and identifies nothing, so Site Name is built by concat of Street + Suburb (e.g. 'STAND NO 507 A507 Mondlo A'); consumer name is kept separately as aba_consumer_name.\n- METER READINGS table: METER NO. / METER TYPE / OLD READING / NEW READING / READING DATE / READING TYPE / CONSUMPTION. One ELECTRICITY meter only on this account ([number removed]). Reading type is a single letter; E, I and N all occur (no A in this set). Mapped by a label_present compute: E->Estimated, A->Actual, I->Interim, N->No Reading. E/A follow the app-wide TRANSLATE convention; I and N are this vendor's codes (I appears with a fresh reading date and a real reading movement, N appears with equal old/new readings and .000 consumption).\n- Only ONE date is printed per meter (READING DATE) -> canonical End Date. There is NO period start/end anywhere on the bill, so Start Date is '_none'. The reading date also LAGS the account date badly (e.g. 13/04/2026 reading on a 22 JUN 2026 statement) and the consumption is a flat 1057.000 for eight consecutive months, i.e. the account is being estimated.\n- ACCOUNT DETAILS ledger: DATE / CODE / DESCRIPTION / UNITS / TARIFF / VALUE. Real tariff-calculated levies carry an '@' between UNITS and TARIFF and a '*' VAT flag before VALUE. Credits print a TRAILING minus (both on the tariff, '0.[number removed]-', and on the value, '558.53-').\n\nLEDGER CODES SEEN\n  110211 RATES / VALUATION REDUCTION / VALAUTION REBATE (bill's own spelling; sometimes suffixed ' 5%' / ' 10%')  -> rates, NOT VAT-flagged\n  080101 REFUSE                                                    -> refuse\n  040203 AVAILABLE WATER BASIC CHARGE                              -> water\n  071292 FLAT RATE WATER CHARGES NO METERS BASIC CHARGE            -> water\n  031101 AVAILABLE SEWER / 030203 AVAILABLE SEWER BASIC CHARGE     -> sewerage\n  061501 WASTE WATER NO CONSUMPTION BASIC CHARGE                   -> sewerage\n  061501 CORRECTION WASTE WATER BILLING (no '@')                    -> sewerage, PRIOR PERIOD\n  054303 / 050301 ELECTRICITY CONSUMPTION (multiple stepped lines) -> electricity energy\n  054303 ELECTRICITY REBATE (with '@', units match the step)       -> electricity energy rebate (negative)\n  954303 DEMAND/SERVICE BASIC CHARGE, 950301 BASIC CHARGE ELECTRICITY -> electricity basic charge\n  954303 CORRECTION ON BASIC ELEC <months> (no '@')                -> electricity, PRIOR PERIOD\n  903301 ELECTRICITY REBATE (no '@', units .000)                    -> electricity, PRIOR PERIOD\n  888801 DIRECT DEPOSIT PAYMENT - THANK YOU / DUPLICATED           -> payments\n  903001 VAT                                                       -> tax line\n\nSTEPPED TARIFF: ELECTRICITY CONSUMPTION prints one line per block (350 @ 3.51 then 707 @ 4.31). collect:'sum' adds the kWh and the Rands; the rebate lines are summed separately and netted into Standard Rands by the aba_std_r compute (they are a per-kWh discount on the same units, not a separate service).\n\nPRIOR-PERIOD LINES - DELIBERATE CHOICE: some statements carry catch-up adjustments dated a day or two BEFORE the account date (b9: eight '903301 ELECTRICITY REBATE' lines totalling -4,295.06 dated 27/01 on a 28 JAN statement, plus six '061501 CORRECTION WASTE WATER BILLING' at -113.06 each; b7: '954303 CORRECTION ON BASIC ELEC JULU 2025 - FEB 2026' -2,040.00). These are re-bills of EARLIER months, so they are EXCLUDED from the current-month electricity buckets (Standard kWh/Rands, Other, Total ex VAT) and captured in their own field aba_prior_elec_adj_r (sewerage: aba_wastewater_corr_r). Reason: this profile feeds per-site monthly electricity cost; folding an eight-month rebate reversal into January would make January's cost meaningless. They ARE part of the VAT base, which is why the VAT identity check uses aba_vatable_r (every '*'-flagged ledger line) and not the electricity buckets.\n  Discriminator is structural, not date arithmetic: current levies always print '@ <tariff>', prior-period adjustments never do.\n\nRULE ZERO / RECONCILE IS CIRCULAR: this bill prints NO per-service subtotal and NO ex-VAT electricity total. total_ex_vat_r is therefore the SUM of the same three parts the Rand columns hold (energy net of rebate + basic charge), so the app's reconcile check is structurally true and proves nothing. The two GENUINE checks are:\n  1. kWh identity: sum(ELECTRICITY CONSUMPTION units) == meter CONSUMPTION == NEW READING - OLD READING. Holds exactly on all 12 bills (aba_cons_kwh vs aba_meter_kwh vs the two reading fields).\n  2. VAT identity: printed '903001 VAT' == 15% of aba_vatable_r (sum of every '*'-flagged ledger line, prior-period adjustments included). Max deviation over the folder 0.03 (rounding).\n\nNOT PRINTED ANYWHERE (mapped '_none'): tariff name, period start date, TOU bands (peak/off-peak), kVA demand, NMD, cash, guarantee, security held. The 'DEMAND/SERVICE BASIC CHARGE' is a flat monthly service charge (units 1.000 @ a rand amount, and the same code prints as 'BASIC CHARGE ELECTRICITY' on the newest bill) - there is no kVA figure anywhere on the statement, so it lands in Other Charges, not Demand Rands.\n\nAgeing row is 6 money columns (120+/90/60/30/CURRENT/CLOSING BALANCE). CURRENT is the net current balance, NOT the current levy - do not use it as 'current charges'. Recon 'current_ex' is therefore left unmapped (the bill prints no ex-VAT current-charges figure).",
